 Format Parameters
 -----------------
-The only supported format parameter is ``constructor``, which specifies the
+The main format parameter is ``constructor``, which specifies the
 type of in-memory sequence object to read each aligned sequence into. This must
 be a subclass of ``GrammaredSequence`` (e.g., ``DNA``, ``RNA``, ``Protein``)
 and is a required format parameter. For example, if you know that the Stockholm
 file you're reading contains DNA sequences, you would pass ``constructor=DNA``
 to the reader call.
 
+Any additional keyword arguments, such as ``lowercase``, are passed to the
+sequence constructor. For example, ``lowercase=True`` allows a file containing
+lowercase sequence characters to be read. If ``lowercase`` is a string, the
+resulting boolean positional metadata column cannot be written back to
+Stockholm format.
+
